=== PARITY (vs web DigitalTwinWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (DigitalTwinSource → DigitalTwinModel):
    useVehicles, useVehicleState, useSecurityLatest, useChargingTelemetryLatest, useTranslation.
    The production app wires DigitalTwinSource over the KMP VehicleStore/SecurityStore/ChargingStore
    (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>>); the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection → buildTwinState + parseDoorState/parseWindowState/parseTurnSignal are a 1:1 port of
    web lib/vehicleState.ts (doors object/enum/string, windows, frunk/trunk derive, charge inference,
    driving/charging heuristics, lock fallback, windowsOpen summary). Verified by executed harness.
  Composition → WidgetShell chrome (Monitor icon + "Digital Twin" title + freshness chip + refresh +
    "Open") · VehicleTwin illustration (doors/windows/lights/lock/sentry/seat/charge overlays,
    drive-in slide + wheel spin) · wrapped+centered Badge row (lock/windows/driving/charging/sentry/
    lights/hazards/doors/frunk/trunk) · vehicle-name footer.
  Shared components → reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion / TSTone / TSSkeleton
    (compiled against the REAL apps/apple component library in the typecheck below). TwinBadge mirrors
    TSBadge/TSStatusPill tokens, extended for the lock glyph + "%lld" counts those shared badges can't
    express. Recharts→none / Leaflet→none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No vehicle data") · error (retry) ·
    stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached value + chip + banner) · content. Model phase resolution
